---
/**
 * /cases/synapse/ — the case study behind the AI rungs. A solo studio with no
 * client logos proves delivery with the strongest artifact it owns: a
 * fine-tuned, self-hosted model running in production on this very site.
 * Problem → constraint → what was built → cost (time) → measured reality →
 * honest limits → bridge to the two AI-track services it proves.
 *
 * The hero is the shared `PageHero` block (`src/components/blocks/`), not a
 * fourteenth hand-typed copy: the whole recipe — plate, eyebrow, letter-split
 * h1, scroll hint, entrance cascade, mobile scroll-hint fix — lives there
 * once. This page passes only what is genuinely its own: the copy, the
 * ComfyUI still generated for it, the direction the scrim darkens, the point
 * the plexus is born from, and where the scroll hint rides to.
 *
 * The still (`src/assets/cases/synapse-hero.png`) landed after the first
 * version of this page was written, which is why the file used to say no
 * photograph existed and rode on `--gradient-hero` instead.
 *
 * The six sections below ARE a narrative arc (problem → constraint → build →
 * cost → result → limits), so they render as the etalon's numbered timeline
 * (Career Arc mechanic) instead of six stacked headings — medallions carry
 * the step number since no per-stage icon set exists for this page.
 */
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import InnerHeader from '@components/layout/InnerHeader.astro';
import PageHero from '@components/blocks/PageHero.astro';
import ServiceCta from '@components/services/ServiceCta.astro';
import heroArt from '@/assets/cases/synapse-hero.png';
import { SITE_ORIGIN } from '@/data/services';
import { breadcrumbNode } from '@/lib/services-jsonld';
import { supportedLangs, t } from '@i18n/utils';
import type { Lang } from '@i18n/utils';
import type { GetStaticPaths } from 'astro';

export const getStaticPaths = (() => {
  return supportedLangs.map((lang) => ({ params: { lang } }));
}) satisfies GetStaticPaths;

const { lang } = Astro.params as { lang: Lang };

const copy = {
  en: {
    title: 'Case: Synapse — a Fine-Tuned Model, No GPU | VKVstudio',
    description:
      'A fine-tuned Gemma model with live RAG, self-hosted on a 4-core ARM server with no GPU at all — the proof behind the RAG-pilot and self-hosted AI services.',
    eyebrow: 'case study',
    h1: 'Synapse: a private assistant with no GPU bill',
    lede: 'The assistant living on this site is not an API wrapper. It is my own fine-tuned model, self-hosted on a modest ARM server, answering with live retrieval — and it exists precisely to prove that this class of system is buildable and affordable.',
    stats: [
      { label: 'Model', value: 'Gemma 4, fine-tuned with QLoRA' },
      { label: 'Hardware', value: '4-core ARM server, no GPU' },
      { label: 'First response', value: '30–45s full answer, words from ~20s' },
    ],
    sections: [
      {
        heading: 'The problem',
        body: 'Every "private AI assistant" pitch runs into the same buyer suspicion: does this actually work without OpenAI behind the curtain, and what does it cost to run for real? The only honest answer is a running system a stranger can poke. So the studio\'s own assistant became the case study: fine-tuned, self-hosted, public — right here on this page.',
      },
      {
        heading: 'The constraint',
        body: "One small rented server, no accelerator — and every constraint a real client brings, stacked on top deliberately: a small open model (Gemma-class, not a frontier API), bilingual EN/RU output, answers grounded in the studio's actual facts rather than the model's imagination, and graceful degradation, because the site has to work in full when the AI box is switched off.",
      },
      {
        heading: 'What was built',
        body: 'A Gemma 4 fine-tuned with QLoRA on a purpose-written dataset — behavior and voice come from the fine-tune, facts come from retrieval (RAG) over a curated knowledge base: tune for form, retrieve for truth. It serves through llama.cpp behind a tunnel, with Google sign-in and a message allowance guarding the expensive path. Chat history lives twice — IndexedDB in the browser, SQLite on the server — kept in sync so a conversation survives closing the tab. And when the box itself is unreachable, the frontend quietly degrades to a scripted mock instead of a broken widget: autonomy by design, not an afterthought.',
      },
      {
        heading: 'What it cost',
        body: "Time, not a number on an invoice. Months of iteration went into a purpose-written training dataset that grew through several generations before the model answering you now was allowed to ship, evaluation gates every candidate had to clear first, and at least one full retrain that failed its own gate and was shelved rather than deployed. Nothing here talks to a real visitor until it passes the same kind of acceptance test a client's own pilot gets — that discipline is the actual cost, and it never shows up as a line item.",
      },
      {
        heading: 'What it does today',
        body: 'On four ARM cores a full first answer takes 30–45 seconds; first words land around the twenty-second mark. Later turns in the same conversation are faster, because the context is already read. That number is published, not hidden — it is the honest price of CPU-only sovereignty at the smallest possible budget. A client deployment sizes hardware to the latency the workflow actually needs; the same architecture on a modest GPU answers in seconds.',
      },
      {
        heading: "What it doesn't do well",
        body: "Three honest limits. It is slow by design — a CPU-bound small model will never race a frontier API, and you feel that on the very first turn. It is narrow, not general — ask it something outside the studio's own knowledge base and retrieval has nothing to hand it, so it says so instead of guessing. And voice is one-way for now: it can speak a reply back with Google's TTS, but transcribing your voice is the piece still unwired — type instead of talking, for the moment.",
      },
    ],
    closingHeading: 'What this proves for your project',
    closingPre:
      'That a fine-tuned small model plus retrieval delivers a domain assistant without per-token bills or data leaving your infrastructure, running on one rented server rather than a GPU cluster — and that the person offering to build yours has already built one in production, in public, with the trade-offs published instead of hidden. Click the brain on the homepage and interrogate it yourself. If your documents need the same treatment, start with the ',
    closingLink1: 'RAG pilot',
    closingMid1:
      ' — a fixed three-week engagement; if compliance means the model has to live on hardware you own outright, that is ',
    closingLink2: 'self-hosted AI',
    closingMid2: '. Both sit on the ',
    closingLink3: 'full price ladder',
    closingPost: '.',
  },
  ru: {
    title: 'Кейс: Synapse — дообученная модель, без GPU | VKVstudio',
    description:
      'Дообученная Gemma с живым RAG, self-hosted на 4-ядерном ARM-сервере совсем без GPU — доказательство за услугами RAG-пилота и self-hosted AI.',
    eyebrow: 'кейс',
    h1: 'Synapse: приватный ассистент без счетов за GPU',
    lede: 'Ассистент, живущий на этом сайте, — не обёртка над API. Это моя собственная дообученная модель, self-hosted на скромном ARM-сервере, отвечающая с живым поиском — и существует она именно как доказательство, что такой класс систем реально построить и потянуть.',
    stats: [
      { label: 'Модель', value: 'Gemma 4, дообучена QLoRA' },
      { label: 'Железо', value: '4-ядерный ARM-сервер, без GPU' },
      // NBSP glues each figure to its unit: inside a 220px tile «30–45» and
      // «с» would otherwise split across lines. (An earlier version of this
      // comment also claimed to fix «слова — с ~20 с» reading as two «с» in
      // a row. It does not — the words were reordered and the pair is still
      // there. NBSP prevents a line break, not an homonym. Whether to reword
      // it, and whether the EN twin should take the same order, is copy.)
      { label: 'Первый ответ', value: 'полный ответ 30–45 с, первые слова — с ~20 с' },
    ],
    sections: [
      {
        heading: 'Задача',
        body: 'Каждое предложение «приватного ИИ-ассистента» упирается в одно и то же подозрение покупателя: это правда работает без OpenAI за кулисами, и сколько это реально стоит в эксплуатации? Единственный честный ответ — работающая система, которую может потыкать посторонний человек. Так ассистент студии стал кейсом: дообученный, self-hosted, публичный — прямо на этой странице.',
      },
      {
        heading: 'Ограничение',
        body: 'Один небольшой арендованный сервер, без ускорителя — и поверх него сознательно положены все ограничения, с которыми приходит реальный клиент: малая открытая модель (класс Gemma, а не frontier-API), двуязычные ответы EN/RU, факты из реальной базы знаний студии, а не из воображения модели, и деградация без драмы — сайт обязан полностью работать, когда ИИ-машина выключена.',
      },
      {
        heading: 'Что построено',
        body: 'Gemma 4, дообученная методом QLoRA на специально написанном датасете: поведение и голос — из файнтюна, факты — из поиска (RAG) по курируемой базе знаний. Тюнинг — для формы, поиск — для правды. Обслуживает её llama.cpp за туннелем, вход через Google и лимит сообщений защищают дорогой путь. История чатов живёт дважды — IndexedDB в браузере, SQLite на сервере — синхронизированно, так что диалог переживает закрытие вкладки. А когда сама машина недоступна, фронтенд тихо деградирует к скриптованному моку вместо сломанного виджета: автономность заложена в архитектуру, а не добавлена потом.',
      },
      {
        heading: 'Что это стоило',
        body: 'Время, а не строка в счёте. Месяцы итераций ушли на специально написанный обучающий датасет, который вырос через несколько поколений, прежде чем модель, отвечающая вам сейчас, получила право выйти в прод; на приёмочные гейты, которые обязан был пройти каждый кандидат; и минимум на одно полное переобучение, которое не прошло свой же гейт и было отложено, а не задеплоено. Здесь ничто не отвечает живому посетителю, пока не пройдёт тот же приёмочный тест, что и клиентский пилот, — эта дисциплина и есть настоящая цена, и в счёте она не значится отдельной строкой.',
      },
      {
        heading: 'Что это делает сегодня',
        body: 'На четырёх ARM-ядрах полный первый ответ занимает 30–45 секунд, первые слова появляются на границе двадцатой секунды. Следующие реплики в том же диалоге быстрее, потому что контекст уже прочитан. Эта цифра опубликована, а не спрятана — это честная цена CPU-суверенитета на минимально возможном бюджете. Клиентское развёртывание подбирает железо под нужную задержку; та же архитектура на скромной GPU-машине отвечает за секунды.',
      },
      {
        heading: 'Что делает плохо',
        body: 'Три честных ограничения. Она медленная по конструкции — CPU-модель такого размера никогда не обгонит frontier-API, и это чувствуется уже на первой реплике. Она узкая, а не универсальная — спросите что-то за пределами базы знаний студии, и поиску нечего подать модели, так что она честно скажет об этом, а не начнёт угадывать. И голос сегодня работает в одну сторону: ответить голосом через Google TTS она может, а вот распознавание вашей речи — та часть, которая ещё не подключена; пока приходится печатать вместо того, чтобы говорить.',
      },
    ],
    closingHeading: 'Что это доказывает для вашего проекта',
    closingPre:
      'Что дообученная малая модель плюс RAG дают доменного ассистента без счетов за каждый токен и без утечки данных с вашей инфраструктуры — и работает это на одном арендованном сервере, а не на GPU-кластере. И что человек, предлагающий построить такого вам, уже построил своего — в продакшне, публично, с опубликованными компромиссами. Кликните по мозгу на главной и допросите его сами. Если вашим документам нужно то же самое — начните с ',
    closingLink1: 'RAG-пилота',
    closingMid1:
      ' — фиксированного трёхнедельного проекта; если комплаенс требует, чтобы модель жила на железе, которым владеете вы, — это ',
    closingLink2: 'self-hosted AI-развёртывание',
    closingMid2: '. Обе ступени — часть ',
    closingLink3: 'полной лестницы цен',
    closingPost: '.',
  },
}[lang];

const pageUrl = `${SITE_ORIGIN}/${lang}/cases/synapse/`;
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: copy.h1,
    description: copy.description,
    url: pageUrl,
    mainEntityOfPage: pageUrl,
    image: `${SITE_ORIGIN}/og-cover${lang === 'ru' ? '-ru' : ''}.jpg`,
    inLanguage: lang,
    author: { '@id': `${SITE_ORIGIN}/#person` },
    publisher: { '@id': `${SITE_ORIGIN}/#organization` },
    datePublished: '2026-08-20',
    dateModified: '2026-08-22',
  },
  breadcrumbNode(lang, [
    { name: t(lang, 'nav.home'), item: `${SITE_ORIGIN}/${lang}/` },
    { name: copy.h1, item: pageUrl },
  ]),
];

// The hero art is this page's LCP element, and PageHero cannot preload it for
// us: an Astro slot does not travel from a nested component up to BaseLayout's
// `head` slot (README, "What it does NOT do"). Widths must match the ones the
// component requests — master is 1280 wide, so [768, 1280] exactly; asking for
// more would clamp, duplicate a URL and buy a second download.
const HERO_WIDTHS = [768, 1280];
const heroPreloads = await Promise.all(
  HERO_WIDTHS.map((width) => getImage({ src: heroArt, format: 'avif', width }))
);
const heroImagesrcset = heroPreloads.map((img, i) => `${img.src} ${HERO_WIDTHS[i]}w`).join(', ');
---

<BaseLayout
  lang={lang}
  title={copy.title}
  description={copy.description}
  ogType="article"
  articlePublished="2026-08-20"
  articleModified="2026-08-22"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <link slot="head" rel="preload" as="image" imagesrcset={heroImagesrcset} imagesizes="100vw" />
  <InnerHeader lang={lang} />
  <main id="main-content" class="case-page">
    {
      /* ── Hero: the shared block. Five page-specific values and nothing else.
         `scrim="center"`: the still's light is a single core in the middle of
         the frame, exactly where the copy sits, so the darkening has to be
         radial and centred — `left` would dim the half that is already black
         and leave the glare under the words.
         `plexus`: the network is born from that same core. The old artless
         hero pointed it at 0.24 / 0.66, a corner chosen when there was no
         picture to be born from; measured on the new master the lit core sits
         at ~0.50 / 0.47, and the anchor pins it there through every crop
         `object-fit: cover` performs. Frame is the master's own 1280×720. */
    }
    <PageHero
      lang={lang}
      eyebrow={copy.eyebrow}
      title={copy.h1}
      lede={copy.lede}
      image={heroArt}
      scrim="center"
      plexus={{
        originX: 0.5,
        originY: 0.47,
        anchor: { x: 0.5, y: 0.47, width: 1280, height: 720 },
      }}
      scrollTarget="#case-body"
    />

    {/* ── At a glance: the three hard numbers, pulled from the copy below ── */}
    <section class="case-stats-section" id="case-body">
      <div class="container">
        <ul class="case-stats" role="list">
          {
            copy.stats.map((s) => (
              <li class="case-stat js-case-stat">
                <span class="case-stat__label text-mono">{s.label}</span>
                <span class="case-stat__value">{s.value}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* ── The arc: problem → constraint → build → cost → result → limits ── */}
    <section class="case-body">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="case-steps-wrap js-case-steps">
          <div class="case-steps__line js-case-steps-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <ol class="case-steps">
            {
              copy.sections.map((s, i) => (
                <li class="case-steps__item js-case-step">
                  <span class="case-steps__dot js-case-step-dot" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span class="text-mono">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
                  </span>
                  <div class="case-steps__card js-case-step-card">
                    <h2>{s.heading}</h2>
                    <p>{s.body}</p>
                  </div>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ol>
        </div>

        <article class="case-closing js-case-reveal">
          <h2>{copy.closingHeading}</h2>
          <p>
            {copy.closingPre}<a href={`/${lang}/services/rag-pilot/`}>{copy.closingLink1}</a>
            {copy.closingMid1}<a href={`/${lang}/services/on-prem-ai/`}>{copy.closingLink2}</a>
            {copy.closingMid2}<a href={`/${lang}/services/`}>{copy.closingLink3}</a>
            {copy.closingPost}
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <ServiceCta lang={lang} />
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // Homepage manners on this page too (owner: they are the site norm) —
  // Lenis smooths the wheel; under reduced motion initLenis() is a no-op.
  import { initLenis } from '@scripts/lenis-init';

  // Motion is an enhancement, never a gatekeeper: nothing here starts hidden
  // in CSS, so a failed import or an old browser sees a complete page.
  // gsap.from() does the hide-then-reveal itself, clearProps hands each
  // element back to the stylesheet once its tween lands.
  async function initCaseMotion(): Promise<void> {
    if (window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return;

    // Cursor parallax on the hero lede — the initGeoHeroManners recipe from
    // services/geo-audit/index.astro, same coefficients as HeroOverlay
    // (nx * -3 / ny * -2). It needs no GSAP, so it lives BEFORE the dynamic
    // import: a failed gsap chunk must not take down a feature that never
    // depended on it. This page's hero is the shared PageHero block, so it
    // targets that markup (`.page-hero` / `.page-hero__lede`). The
    // reduced-motion gate is the early return above; the hover/pointer gate
    // below is the recipe's own second gate — a touch device has no cursor.
    if (window.matchMedia('(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)').matches) {
      const hero = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.page-hero');
      const lede = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.page-hero__lede');
      if (hero && lede) {
        hero.addEventListener(
          'mousemove',
          (e) => {
            const r = hero.getBoundingClientRect();
            const x = (e.clientX - r.left) / r.width;
            const y = (e.clientY - r.top) / r.height;
            lede.style.transform = `translate(${(x - 0.5) * -3}px, ${(y - 0.5) * -2}px)`;
          },
          { passive: true }
        );

        hero.addEventListener('mouseleave', () => {
          lede.style.transform = '';
        });
      }
    }

    try {
      const [{ gsap }, { ScrollTrigger }] = await Promise.all([
        import('gsap'),
        import('gsap/ScrollTrigger'),
      ]);
      gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);

      // One row of identical tiles is ONE wave, not three independent ones:
      // the trigger sits on the container and `stagger` deals the cards out.
      // Values are the site's own "tile appears" recipe (geo-audit's
      // js-geo-tile / section-animations.ts), not a local invention.
      const statTiles = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.js-case-stat'));
      if (statTiles.length) {
        gsap.fromTo(
          statTiles,
          { opacity: 0, y: 50, scale: 0.92 },
          {
            opacity: 1,
            y: 0,
            scale: 1,
            duration: 0.7,
            ease: 'expo.out',
            stagger: 0.08,
            clearProps: 'all',
            scrollTrigger: { trigger: '.case-stats', start: 'top 80%' },
          }
        );
      }

      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.js-case-reveal').forEach((el) => {
        gsap.from(el, {
          opacity: 0,
          y: 24,
          duration: 0.7,
          ease: 'power2.out',
          clearProps: 'all',
          scrollTrigger: { trigger: el, start: 'top 88%' },
        });
      });

      // The arc: the Career Arc's own "neural signal propagation" mechanic,
      // verbatim from initAboutAnimations / the geo-audit process timeline.
      // The line's real span is baked in as inline top/height (first-dot-
      // center → last-dot-center), then its scaleY is scrubbed; each step
      // springs its numbered medallion and slides its card out of a blur.
      const stepsWrap = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.js-case-steps');
      if (stepsWrap) {
        const line = stepsWrap.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.js-case-steps-line');
        const dots = stepsWrap.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.js-case-step-dot');
        const firstDot = dots[0];
        const lastDot = dots[dots.length - 1];

        if (line && firstDot && lastDot && dots.length >= 2) {
          const wrapRect = stepsWrap.getBoundingClientRect();
          const firstRect = firstDot.getBoundingClientRect();
          const lastRect = lastDot.getBoundingClientRect();
          const lineTop = firstRect.top - wrapRect.top + firstRect.height / 2;
          const lineHeight = lastRect.top - wrapRect.top + lastRect.height / 2 - lineTop;
          line.style.top = `${lineTop}px`;
          line.style.height = `${lineHeight}px`;
          line.style.bottom = 'auto';

          gsap.fromTo(
            line,
            { scaleY: 0 },
            {
              scaleY: 1,
              ease: 'none',
              scrollTrigger: {
                trigger: stepsWrap,
                start: 'top 75%',
                end: 'bottom 40%',
                scrub: 0.8,
              },
            }
          );
        }

        stepsWrap.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.js-case-step').forEach((item) => {
          const dot = item.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.js-case-step-dot');
          const card = item.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.js-case-step-card');

          const itemTl = gsap.timeline({
            scrollTrigger: {
              trigger: item,
              start: 'top 78%',
              toggleActions: 'play none none none',
            },
          });

          if (dot) {
            itemTl.fromTo(
              dot,
              { scale: 0, boxShadow: '0 0 0px transparent' },
              {
                scale: 1,
                boxShadow: '0 0 20px hsla(155, 70%, 50%, 0.4)',
                duration: 0.6,
                ease: 'back.out(2.5)',
                onComplete: () => {
                  dot.classList.add('is-active');
                },
              },
              0
            );
          }

          if (card) {
            itemTl.fromTo(
              card,
              { opacity: 0, x: -30, filter: 'blur(6px)' },
              { opacity: 1, x: 0, filter: 'blur(0px)', duration: 0.7, ease: 'expo.out' },
              // 0.25, not 0.15: the site's step rhythm is dot 0 → icon 0.15 →
              // card 0.25. This page has no icon, but dropping its slot moved
              // the card a beat early against every other timeline.
              0.25
            );
          }
        });
      }
    } catch (err) {
      // No rescue pass needed — content was never hidden.
      console.error('[case-synapse] motion failed to load:', err);
    }
  }

  // The scroll hint is PageHero's own behaviour now (it reads the same
  // window.lenisInstance initLenis() publishes below), so nothing about it is
  // wired here any more.
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
      initLenis();
      void initCaseMotion();
    });
  } else {
    initLenis();
    void initCaseMotion();
  }
</script>

<style>
  .case-page {
    padding-top: var(--space-10);
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: var(--bg-obsidian);
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .case-page {
      padding-top: var(--space-4);
    }
  }

  /* The hero's own rules used to live here — the whole `.case-hero*` family,
     its six keyframe sets and the mobile scroll-hint fix. They moved into
     `src/components/blocks/PageHero.astro` unchanged in intent; nothing on
     this page references those class names any more. */

  /* ── At-a-glance stat strip — the Lab card recipe, three hard numbers
     pulled verbatim from the arc below, read in five seconds. ─────────── */
  .case-stats-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-10) var(--space-4);
  }

  .case-stats {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-5);
    max-width: var(--container-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .case-stat {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    background: var(--glass-bg);
    backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur));
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur));
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow);
    text-align: center;
    /* Named properties, never `all`: GSAP tweens opacity/y/scale on this very
       element, and a blanket 250ms transition would re-ease every frame of the
       entrance tween. One element, one animator. */
    transition:
      border-color var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-out),
      box-shadow var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-out);
  }

  /* Standard property restated where a CSS minifier cannot fold it into
     the -webkit- alias — without this Firefox renders it flat. */
  @supports (backdrop-filter: blur(1px)) {
    .case-stat {
      backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur));
    }
  }

  .case-stat:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent-green-300);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow), var(--glow-green);
  }

  /* The lift is motion, not a colour shift — so it lives entirely behind
     reduced-motion, exactly as on PricingCard: those visitors get the same
     card with a colour-only hover, never a forced translate. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .case-stat {
      transition:
        border-color var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-out),
        box-shadow var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-out),
        transform var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-out);
    }

    .case-stat:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }
  }

  .case-stat__label {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    color: var(--accent-green-400);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .case-stat__value {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .case-body {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  /* ── The arc — the Career Arc mechanic verbatim, medallions carrying a
     step number instead of an icon (no per-stage icon set for this page). */
  .case-steps-wrap {
    position: relative;
    max-width: var(--container-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .case-steps__line {
    position: absolute;
    left: 19px;
    top: 20px;
    bottom: 20px;
    width: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      var(--accent-green-300),
      var(--accent-green-500) 50%,
      var(--accent-green-300)
    );
    transform-origin: top center;
    z-index: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .case-steps__line {
      left: 23px;
    }
  }

  .case-steps {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    position: relative;
  }

  .case-steps__item {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .case-steps__item {
      gap: var(--space-8);
    }
  }

  .case-steps__item:last-child {
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .case-steps__dot {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    background: var(--bg-graphite);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--accent-green-300);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    color: var(--accent-green-200);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 transparent;
    z-index: 2;
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .case-steps__dot {
      width: 48px;
      height: 48px;
    }
  }

  .case-steps__dot.is-active {
    animation: case-dot-pulse 2.5s ease-in-out 0.6s infinite;
  }

  @keyframes case-dot-pulse {
    0%,
    100% {
      box-shadow:
        0 0 12px var(--accent-glow),
        0 0 0 0 hsla(155, 70%, 50%, 0.3);
    }
    50% {
      box-shadow:
        0 0 20px var(--accent-glow-strong),
        0 0 0 8px hsla(155, 70%, 50%, 0);
    }
  }

  .case-steps__card {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
    background: var(--glass-bg);
    backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur));
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur));
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow);
    transition:
      border-color var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-out),
      box-shadow var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-out);
  }

  /* Standard property restated where a CSS minifier cannot fold it into
     the -webkit- alias — without this Firefox renders it flat. */
  @supports (backdrop-filter: blur(1px)) {
    .case-steps__card {
      backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur));
    }
  }

  .case-steps__card:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent-green-300);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow), var(--glow-green);
  }

  .case-steps__card h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .case-steps__card p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal, 1.7);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Closing bridge — the callout idiom, so the last argument reads as a
     destination, not a seventh identical block. ───────────────────────── */
  .case-closing {
    max-width: var(--container-narrow);
    margin: var(--space-12) auto 0;
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-6) var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-green-300);
    background: var(--glass-bg);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-lg) var(--radius-lg) 0;
  }

  .case-closing h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .case-closing p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Bridge links — underlined, not color-only, matching ServiceCta's own
     inline-link recipe. */
  .case-closing p a {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    transition: var(--transition-colors);
  }

  .case-closing p a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-green-300);
  }
</style>
